window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b271-922ea7cf3eaba36b.json"]={sha256:"922ea7cf3eaba36b0e5f47d628c4161c93e5b9963026093d33157b99d6e8aa6c",value:{"id":"b271","title":"都市滯洪池配置","titleEn":"Urban detention-basin planning","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"課程從連通集水區和事件體積進入儲量演算，逐項建立池容、孔口、溢流、滲透與排空模型，最後檢查下游峰時、沉積和數值閉合。大坑東與跑馬地提供地下蓄洪實例，全部數值為合成假設；規劃的核心是保存水量與確認去向，不把單一削峰百分比當完整防洪成效。","summaryEn":"The course moves from connected catchment and event volume into storage routing, geometry, orifices, overflow, infiltration and drawdown, then checks downstream timing, sediment and numerical closure. Tai Hang Tung and Happy Valley provide underground-storage examples. All numbers are synthetic assumptions; planning centers on conservation and destination rather than treating one peak-reduction percentage as complete flood performance.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-river","architectureNodes":[["連通集水區","Connected catchment"],["入流歷線","Inflow hydrograph"],["儲量與出口","Storage and outlet"],["下游匯流","Downstream combination"],["維護與驗證","Maintenance and verification"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]],"diagram":{"type":"water-river","labels":["連通集水區","入流歷線","儲量與出口","下游匯流","維護與驗證"],"labelsEn":["Connected catchment","Inflow hydrograph","Storage and outlet","Downstream combination","Maintenance and verification"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"敏感度固定孔口係數Cd=0.62與兩側水頭差1.0 m，只把圓孔直徑增加10%。面積和瞬時流量都增加21%，若原開口0.10 m²的流量為0.2746 m³/s，新面積0.121 m²對應0.3323 m³/s。這可能較快恢復池容，但也可能增加下游負荷；在同一固定池面積及自由排水積分模型下，排空時間因面積增加而降為原值的82.64%。實際事件的水位會隨出流改變，尾水和部分淹沒也可能變動，因此不能直接用固定水頭比例取代全歷線重算。","textEn":"For sensitivity, hold Cd=0.62 and differential head at 1.0 m while increasing circular-orifice diameter by ten percent. Area and instantaneous discharge both rise by 21%. An original 0.10 m² opening releases 0.2746 m³/s; the new 0.121 m² opening releases 0.3323 m³/s. This can restore storage sooner but also increases downstream loading. Under the same constant-area, free-drawdown integral model, time falls to 82.64% of its original value. Real event stage responds to release, while tailwater and submergence may change. The fixed-head ratio therefore cannot replace rerouting the complete hydrograph.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b271-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證」與「歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification\" and \"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b271-v15-01","title":"集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「集水區與逕流體積」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Catchment and runoff volume” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"滯洪池的第一個問題是哪些地表真正連到入口，而不是行政邊界內有多少面積。屋頂、道路和透水地的產流不同，前期含水與管網分流又會改變有效貢獻；事件總量可用簡化係數作初估，但它沒有提供洪峰出現時間或歷線形狀，不能單靠總雨量完成池容設計。本例係數為指定事件的體積比例，假設雨量均勻且無跨區來水；它不是用於求瞬時洪峰的完整理性式分析。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「集水區與逕流體積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The first detention question is which surfaces actually connect to the inlet, not how much area lies inside an administrative boundary. Roofs, roads and permeable land generate different runoff, while antecedent wetness and network diversion change effective contribution. An event coefficient provides an initial volume estimate but not crest timing or hydrograph shape, so rainfall total alone cannot size the basin. The coefficient is a specified event-volume fraction under uniform rainfall and no imported flow. This is not a complete rational-method peak-flow analysis. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Catchment and runoff volume” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件雨量P=0.050 m、連通面積A=200000 m²、體積逕流係數C=0.70，V=CPA=7000 m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event rainfall P=0.050 m, connected area A=200000 m² and volume runoff coefficient C=0.70.","failure":"常見誤解：「知道總雨量與總面積後，就能唯一決定所需滯洪池容量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Total rainfall and total area uniquely determine the required detention capacity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「集水區與逕流體積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Catchment and runoff volume”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-01-k1","title":"集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證","titleEn":"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification","text":"滯洪池的第一個問題是哪些地表真正連到入口，而不是行政邊界內有多少面積。屋頂、道路和透水地的產流不同，前期含水與管網分流又會改變有效貢獻；事件總量可用簡化係數作初估，但它沒有提供洪峰出現時間或歷線形狀，不能單靠總雨量完成池容設計。","textEn":"The first detention question is which surfaces actually connect to the inlet, not how much area lies inside an administrative boundary. Roofs, roads and permeable land generate different runoff, while antecedent wetness and network diversion change effective contribution.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：知道總雨量與總面積後，就能唯一決定所需滯洪池容量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Total rainfall and total area uniquely determine the required detention capacity. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["知道總雨量與總面積後，就能唯一決定所需滯洪池容量。","滯洪池的第一個問題是哪些地表真正連到入口，而不是行政邊界內有多少面積。","所需滯洪容積就是最大入流減去最大出流，不需要積分時間。"],"optionsEn":["Total rainfall and total area uniquely determine the required detention capacity.","The first detention question is which surfaces actually connect to the inlet, not how much area lies inside an administrative boundary.","Required detention volume is maximum inflow minus maximum outflow without time integration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"滯洪池的第一個問題是哪些地表真正連到入口，而不是行政邊界內有多少面積。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The first detention question is which surfaces actually connect to the inlet, not how much area lies inside an administrative boundary. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b271-v15-02","title":"集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「集水區與逕流體積」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Catchment and runoff volume” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件雨量P=0.050 m、連通面積A=200000 m²、體積逕流係數C=0.70，V=CPA=7000 m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event rainfall P=0.050 m, connected area A=200000 m² and volume runoff coefficient C=0.70. Runoff V=CPA=7000 m³. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以排水連通調查核對有效面積，將雨量與入口事件體積比較，分開記錄跨區分流和前期含水。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Verify connected area through drainage mapping and compare rainfall with measured inlet event volume, recording imported flow and antecedent wetness separately.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件雨量P=0.050 m、連通面積A=200000 m²、體積逕流係數C=0.70，V=CPA=7000 m³。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event rainfall P=0.050 m, connected area A=200000 m² and volume runoff coefficient C=0.70. Runoff V=CPA=7000 m³.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["孔口流量只和池內水深有關，下游水位升高不會影響。","透水池底的入滲率永遠固定，因此可以無條件扣減所需池容。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件雨量P=0.050 m、連通面積A=200000 m²、體積逕流係數C=0.70，V=CPA=7000 m³。"],"optionsEn":["Orifice discharge depends only on basin depth and is unaffected by downstream water level.","A permeable floor has constant infiltration that can always be deducted from required storage.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event rainfall P=0.050 m, connected area A=200000 m² and volume runoff coefficient C=0.70."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件雨量P=0.050 m、連通面積A=200000 m²、體積逕流係數C=0.70，V=CPA=7000 m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event rainfall P=0.050 m, connected area A=200000 m² and volume runoff coefficient C=0.70. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b271-v15-03","title":"集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「集水區與逕流體積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Catchment and runoff volume” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以排水連通調查核對有效面積，將雨量與入口事件體積比較，分開記錄跨區分流和前期含水。檢查係數是否隨事件改變，並補上時間分布資料才能進行真正的滯洪演算。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Verify connected area through drainage mapping and compare rainfall with measured inlet event volume, recording imported flow and antecedent wetness separately. Check event-to-event coefficient changes and obtain temporal distribution before using the volume estimate in actual detention routing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：畫出行政界和實際排水界，辨認一條跨界管線對體積帳的影響。為相同事件雨量安排兩種時間分布，說明為何後續必須比較完整入流歷線。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw administrative and drainage boundaries and identify the effect of one cross-boundary pipe on the volume ledger. Arrange two temporal patterns for equal rainfall and explain why complete inflow hydrographs must subsequently be compared.","failure":"注意干擾：把整個集水區都當不透水會高估部分情境，漏掉管網跨區來水則可能低估；即使事件總量正確，不同雨型仍可能產生完全不同的峰值與需要庫容。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating the whole catchment as impervious overestimates some cases, while omitted network imports underestimate others. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以排水連通調查核對有效面積，將雨量與入口事件體積比較，分開記錄跨區分流和前期含水。檢查係數是否隨事件改變，並補上時間分布資料才能進行真正的滯洪演算。","textEn":"Verify connected area through drainage mapping and compare rainfall with measured inlet event volume, recording imported flow and antecedent wetness separately. Check event-to-event coefficient changes and obtain temporal distribution before using the volume estimate in actual detention routing.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"畫出行政界和實際排水界，辨認一條跨界管線對體積帳的影響。為相同事件雨量安排兩種時間分布，說明為何後續必須比較完整入流歷線。","textEn":"Draw administrative and drainage boundaries and identify the effect of one cross-boundary pipe on the volume ledger. Arrange two temporal patterns for equal rainfall and explain why complete inflow hydrographs must subsequently be compared.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification\"?","options":["以排水連通調查核對有效面積，將雨量與入口事件體積比較，分開記錄跨區分流和前期含水。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","每座滯洪池都降低自己的出口峰值，就能保證最下游峰值同比降低。"],"optionsEn":["Verify connected area through drainage mapping and compare rainfall with measured inlet event volume, recording imported flow and antecedent wetness separately.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Reducing each basin outlet peak guarantees the same proportional reduction at the downstream terminus."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以排水連通調查核對有效面積，將雨量與入口事件體積比較，分開記錄跨區分流和前期含水。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Verify connected area through drainage mapping and compare rainfall with measured inlet event volume, recording imported flow and antecedent wetness separately. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b271-v15-04","title":"集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「集水區與逕流體積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Catchment and runoff volume” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把整個集水區都當不透水會高估部分情境，漏掉管網跨區來水則可能低估；即使事件總量正確，不同雨型仍可能產生完全不同的峰值與需要庫容。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating the whole catchment as impervious overestimates some cases, while omitted network imports underestimate others. Even a correct event volume can produce very different peaks and storage requirements under different rainfall timing. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例係數為指定事件的體積比例，假設雨量均勻且無跨區來水；它不是用於求瞬時洪峰的完整理性式分析。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This is not a complete rational-method peak-flow analysis.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「知道總雨量與總面積後，就能唯一決定所需滯洪池容量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Total rainfall and total area uniquely determine the required detention capacity.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把整個集水區都當不透水會高估部分情境，漏掉管網跨區來水則可能低估；即使事件總量正確，不同雨型仍可能產生完全不同的峰值與需要庫容。","textEn":"Treating the whole catchment as impervious overestimates some cases, while omitted network imports underestimate others. Even a correct event volume can produce very different peaks and storage requirements under different rainfall timing.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「集水區與逕流體積機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Catchment and runoff volume mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把整個集水區都當不透水會高估部分情境，漏掉管網跨區來水則可能低估；即使事件總量正確，不同雨型仍可能產生完全不同的峰值與需要庫容。","所需滯洪容積就是最大入流減去最大出流，不需要積分時間。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Treating the whole catchment as impervious overestimates some cases, while omitted network imports underestimate others.","Required detention volume is maximum inflow minus maximum outflow without time integration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把整個集水區都當不透水會高估部分情境，漏掉管網跨區來水則可能低估；即使事件總量正確，不同雨型仍可能產生完全不同的峰值與需要庫容。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating the whole catchment as impervious overestimates some cases, while omitted network imports underestimate others. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b271-v15-05","title":"歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「歷線演算與儲量變化」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Hydrograph routing and storage change” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"滯洪利用進出流量的時間差暫存水量，所需最大庫容來自累積差額而不是洪峰流量相減。出口流量又依池水位與下游水位變化，使儲量和出流彼此耦合；若只固定一個出流上限而不限制可用水量，演算可能在池空時仍排水，產生不可能的負儲量。本例以一個時間步的已知端點流量作梯形積分，假設步內線性變化且儲量足夠；未求完整水位依存出口。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「歷線演算與儲量變化」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Detention stores the time-integrated difference between inflow and outflow, not the difference of peak discharges alone. Outlet flow depends on basin and downstream stages, coupling storage and release. A fixed outflow cap without water-availability constraints can continue releasing from an empty basin and create physically impossible negative storage. The example trapezoidally integrates known endpoint flows over one step, assuming linear variation and sufficient water. It does not solve a complete stage-dependent outlet. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Hydrograph routing and storage change” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δt=300 s、入流I1=4、I2=6及出流O1=2、O2=3 m³/s，ΔS=[(I1+I2)−(O1+O2)]Δt/2=750 m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δt=300 s, inflows I1=4, I2=6 and outflows O1=2, O2=3 m³/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「所需滯洪容積就是最大入流減去最大出流，不需要積分時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Required detention volume is maximum inflow minus maximum outflow without time integration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「歷線演算與儲量變化」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Hydrograph routing and storage change”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-05-k1","title":"歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證","titleEn":"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification","text":"滯洪利用進出流量的時間差暫存水量，所需最大庫容來自累積差額而不是洪峰流量相減。出口流量又依池水位與下游水位變化，使儲量和出流彼此耦合；若只固定一個出流上限而不限制可用水量，演算可能在池空時仍排水，產生不可能的負儲量。","textEn":"Detention stores the time-integrated difference between inflow and outflow, not the difference of peak discharges alone. Outlet flow depends on basin and downstream stages, coupling storage and release.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所需滯洪容積就是最大入流減去最大出流，不需要積分時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Required detention volume is maximum inflow minus maximum outflow without time integration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["所需滯洪容積就是最大入流減去最大出流，不需要積分時間。","池頂平面面積乘總深度永遠等於可用滯洪容量。","滯洪利用進出流量的時間差暫存水量，所需最大庫容來自累積差額而不是洪峰流量相減。"],"optionsEn":["Required detention volume is maximum inflow minus maximum outflow without time integration.","Top plan area times total depth always equals usable detention storage.","Detention stores the time-integrated difference between inflow and outflow, not the difference of peak discharges alone."],"answer":2,"explanation":"滯洪利用進出流量的時間差暫存水量，所需最大庫容來自累積差額而不是洪峰流量相減。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Detention stores the time-integrated difference between inflow and outflow, not the difference of peak discharges alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b271-v15-06","title":"歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「歷線演算與儲量變化」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Hydrograph routing and storage change” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δt=300 s、入流I1=4、I2=6及出流O1=2、O2=3 m³/s，ΔS=[(I1+I2)−(O1+O2)]Δt/2=750 m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δt=300 s, inflows I1=4, I2=6 and outflows O1=2, O2=3 m³/s. Storage change ΔS=[(I1+I2)−(O1+O2)]Δt/2=750 m³. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐步核對入流、出流、初始和最終儲量，確認流量時間戳與積分區間一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconcile inflow, outflow and initial/final storage step by step, aligning timestamps with integration intervals.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δt=300 s、入流I1=4、I2=6及出流O1=2、O2=3 m³/s，ΔS=[(I1+I2)−(O1+O2)]Δt/2=750 m³。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δt=300 s, inflows I1=4, I2=6 and outflows O1=2, O2=3 m³/s. Storage change ΔS=[(I1+I2)−(O1+O2)]Δt/2=750 m³.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δt=300 s、入流I1=4、I2=6及出流O1=2、O2=3 m³/s，ΔS=[(I1+I2)−(O1+O2)]Δt/2=750 m³。","只要設置溢流堰，超量洪水就已經有安全去處而不必追蹤。","孔口排空時間可永遠用總水量除以一開始的最大出流量。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δt=300 s, inflows I1=4, I2=6 and outflows O1=2, O2=3 m³/s.","An overflow weir automatically gives excess floodwater a safe destination without route analysis.","Orifice drawdown time always equals total water volume divided by the initial maximum release."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Δt=300 s、入流I1=4、I2=6及出流O1=2、O2=3 m³/s，ΔS=[(I1+I2)−(O1+O2)]Δt/2=750 m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Δt=300 s, inflows I1=4, I2=6 and outflows O1=2, O2=3 m³/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b271-v15-07","title":"歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「歷線演算與儲量變化」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Hydrograph routing and storage change” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐步核對入流、出流、初始和最終儲量，確認流量時間戳與積分區間一致。縮小時間步比較最大水位及峰值時刻，並檢查池空、滿溢與逆流時的邊界切換是否守恆。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconcile inflow, outflow and initial/final storage step by step, aligning timestamps with integration intervals. Reduce the time step to compare maximum stage and crest timing, and check conservation when boundaries switch at empty storage, overflow or reverse flow. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用四個時間步建立累積儲量，讓最後一步可能排空並修正不可能出流。將修正前後的總水量比較，指出負儲量不是可接受的數值小誤差。","observationEn":"Site practice: Build cumulative storage over four steps, allowing the last to empty the basin and correcting impossible outflow. Compare total water before and after correction and explain why negative storage is not an acceptable small numerical error.","failure":"注意干擾：將立方公尺每秒差額直接當池容積會漏掉時間量綱，過大時間步又可能跨過短時峰值；未處理池空邊界會製造不存在的排水量和虛假削峰效益。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using a discharge difference as storage omits time dimensions, and overly large steps can skip a brief peak. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐步核對入流、出流、初始和最終儲量，確認流量時間戳與積分區間一致。縮小時間步比較最大水位及峰值時刻，並檢查池空、滿溢與逆流時的邊界切換是否守恆。","textEn":"Reconcile inflow, outflow and initial/final storage step by step, aligning timestamps with integration intervals. Reduce the time step to compare maximum stage and crest timing, and check conservation when boundaries switch at empty storage, overflow or reverse flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用四個時間步建立累積儲量，讓最後一步可能排空並修正不可能出流。將修正前後的總水量比較，指出負儲量不是可接受的數值小誤差。","textEn":"Build cumulative storage over four steps, allowing the last to empty the basin and correcting impossible outflow. Compare total water before and after correction and explain why negative storage is not an acceptable small numerical error.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","逐步核對入流、出流、初始和最終儲量，確認流量時間戳與積分區間一致。","只要沉積占總池容比例很小，出口與滯洪效能就不可能受影響。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Reconcile inflow, outflow and initial/final storage step by step, aligning timestamps with integration intervals.","A small deposited fraction of total storage cannot affect the outlet or detention performance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"逐步核對入流、出流、初始和最終儲量，確認流量時間戳與積分區間一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconcile inflow, outflow and initial/final storage step by step, aligning timestamps with integration intervals. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b271-v15-08","title":"歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「歷線演算與儲量變化」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Hydrograph routing and storage change” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將立方公尺每秒差額直接當池容積會漏掉時間量綱，過大時間步又可能跨過短時峰值；未處理池空邊界會製造不存在的排水量和虛假削峰效益。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using a discharge difference as storage omits time dimensions, and overly large steps can skip a brief peak. Missing the empty-basin boundary invents discharge and produces a false attenuation benefit. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例以一個時間步的已知端點流量作梯形積分，假設步內線性變化且儲量足夠；未求完整水位依存出口。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It does not solve a complete stage-dependent outlet.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所需滯洪容積就是最大入流減去最大出流，不需要積分時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Required detention volume is maximum inflow minus maximum outflow without time integration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將立方公尺每秒差額直接當池容積會漏掉時間量綱，過大時間步又可能跨過短時峰值；未處理池空邊界會製造不存在的排水量和虛假削峰效益。","textEn":"Using a discharge difference as storage omits time dimensions, and overly large steps can skip a brief peak. Missing the empty-basin boundary invents discharge and produces a false attenuation benefit.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「歷線演算與儲量變化機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Hydrograph routing and storage change mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","池頂平面面積乘總深度永遠等於可用滯洪容量。","將立方公尺每秒差額直接當池容積會漏掉時間量綱，過大時間步又可能跨過短時峰值；未處理池空邊界會製造不存在的排水量和虛假削峰效益。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Top plan area times total depth always equals usable detention storage.","Using a discharge difference as storage omits time dimensions, and overly large steps can skip a brief peak."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將立方公尺每秒差額直接當池容積會漏掉時間量綱，過大時間步又可能跨過短時峰值；未處理池空邊界會製造不存在的排水量和虛假削峰效益。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using a discharge difference as storage omits time dimensions, and overly large steps can skip a brief peak. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b271-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證」與「孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification\" and \"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b271-v15-09","title":"水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「水位面積與有效池容」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Stage area and usable storage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"滯洪池的平面面積可隨水位增加，邊坡、柱體及設備又會改變有效蓄水空間。面積曲線積分才得到庫容，不能用最高水位面積乘水深代替所有幾何；永久水池、沉砂區與不可抽空部分也應從可用調洪容積分開，避免以總挖方體積宣稱防洪能力。本例採線性水位面積關係且從指定空池基準積分，未含柱體或死水容積；實際幾何需由測量和竣工資料建立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水位面積與有效池容」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Basin surface area may grow with stage, while slopes, columns and equipment alter usable space. Integrating the area curve yields storage; maximum surface area times depth does not represent all geometries. Permanent pools, sediment reserves and undrainable zones must also be separated from available flood storage instead of equating excavation volume with flood capacity. The example integrates a linear stage-area relation from a specified empty datum, excluding columns and dead storage. Actual geometry needs survey and as-built records. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Stage area and usable storage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設A(h)=1000+200h m²，其中h以m計；到h=2 m的庫容S=1000h+100h²=2400 m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume A(h)=1000+200h m² with h in meters.","failure":"常見誤解：「池頂平面面積乘總深度永遠等於可用滯洪容量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Top plan area times total depth always equals usable detention storage.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「水位面積與有效池容」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Stage area and usable storage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-09-k1","title":"水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證","titleEn":"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification","text":"滯洪池的平面面積可隨水位增加，邊坡、柱體及設備又會改變有效蓄水空間。面積曲線積分才得到庫容，不能用最高水位面積乘水深代替所有幾何；永久水池、沉砂區與不可抽空部分也應從可用調洪容積分開，避免以總挖方體積宣稱防洪能力。","textEn":"Basin surface area may grow with stage, while slopes, columns and equipment alter usable space. Integrating the area curve yields storage; maximum surface area times depth does not represent all geometries.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：池頂平面面積乘總深度永遠等於可用滯洪容量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Top plan area times total depth always equals usable detention storage. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["滯洪池的平面面積可隨水位增加，邊坡、柱體及設備又會改變有效蓄水空間。","池頂平面面積乘總深度永遠等於可用滯洪容量。","孔口流量只和池內水深有關，下游水位升高不會影響。"],"optionsEn":["Basin surface area may grow with stage, while slopes, columns and equipment alter usable space.","Top plan area times total depth always equals usable detention storage.","Orifice discharge depends only on basin depth and is unaffected by downstream water level."],"answer":0,"explanation":"滯洪池的平面面積可隨水位增加，邊坡、柱體及設備又會改變有效蓄水空間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Basin surface area may grow with stage, while slopes, columns and equipment alter usable space. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b271-v15-10","title":"水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「水位面積與有效池容」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Stage area and usable storage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設A(h)=1000+200h m²，其中h以m計；到h=2 m的庫容S=1000h+100h²=2400 m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume A(h)=1000+200h m² with h in meters. Storage at h=2 m is S=1000h+100h²=2400 m³. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對面積曲線的標高基準與插值方式，將分層積分容積和三維幾何模型比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check elevation datum and interpolation of the area curve, comparing layered integration with three-dimensional geometry.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設A(h)=1000+200h m²，其中h以m計；到h=2 m的庫容S=1000h+100h²=2400 m³。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume A(h)=1000+200h m² with h in meters. Storage at h=2 m is S=1000h+100h²=2400 m³.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["透水池底的入滲率永遠固定，因此可以無條件扣減所需池容。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設A(h)=1000+200h m²，其中h以m計；到h=2 m的庫容S=1000h+100h²=2400 m³。","每座滯洪池都降低自己的出口峰值，就能保證最下游峰值同比降低。"],"optionsEn":["A permeable floor has constant infiltration that can always be deducted from required storage.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume A(h)=1000+200h m² with h in meters.","Reducing each basin outlet peak guarantees the same proportional reduction at the downstream terminus."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設A(h)=1000+200h m²，其中h以m計；到h=2 m的庫容S=1000h+100h²=2400 m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume A(h)=1000+200h m² with h in meters. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b271-v15-11","title":"水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水位面積與有效池容」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Stage area and usable storage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對面積曲線的標高基準與插值方式，將分層積分容積和三維幾何模型比較。另列永久水位、沉積及構件占用，確認演算使用可動用的庫容，而不是圖面標示的總空間。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check elevation datum and interpolation of the area curve, comparing layered integration with three-dimensional geometry. List permanent water, deposits and structural displacement separately, confirming that routing uses accessible storage rather than the gross space labeled on a drawing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：對線性面積曲線做分層與解析兩種積分，再扣除一個假設永久水位以下體積。說明最高水位不變時，初始積水如何減少可用調洪容量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Integrate the linear area curve numerically and analytically, then subtract volume below a hypothetical permanent level. Explain how initial water reduces available flood storage even when the maximum permitted stage is unchanged.","failure":"注意干擾：用頂面積乘深度會對向上擴張池體高估容積，漏掉柱體或既有積水也會虛增可用量；基準不一致時甚至可能把同一段水深重複計入。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Multiplying top area by depth overstates storage in an expanding basin. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對面積曲線的標高基準與插值方式，將分層積分容積和三維幾何模型比較。另列永久水位、沉積及構件占用，確認演算使用可動用的庫容，而不是圖面標示的總空間。","textEn":"Check elevation datum and interpolation of the area curve, comparing layered integration with three-dimensional geometry. List permanent water, deposits and structural displacement separately, confirming that routing uses accessible storage rather than the gross space labeled on a drawing.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"對線性面積曲線做分層與解析兩種積分，再扣除一個假設永久水位以下體積。說明最高水位不變時，初始積水如何減少可用調洪容量。","textEn":"Integrate the linear area curve numerically and analytically, then subtract volume below a hypothetical permanent level. Explain how initial water reduces available flood storage even when the maximum permitted stage is unchanged.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","模型水量誤差很小，就等於峰值水位和所有設計判斷都正確。","核對面積曲線的標高基準與插值方式，將分層積分容積和三維幾何模型比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A small model water-balance error proves correct peak stage and every design decision.","Check elevation datum and interpolation of the area curve, comparing layered integration with three-dimensional geometry."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對面積曲線的標高基準與插值方式，將分層積分容積和三維幾何模型比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check elevation datum and interpolation of the area curve, comparing layered integration with three-dimensional geometry. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b271-v15-12","title":"水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「水位面積與有效池容」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Stage area and usable storage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用頂面積乘深度會對向上擴張池體高估容積，漏掉柱體或既有積水也會虛增可用量；基準不一致時甚至可能把同一段水深重複計入。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Multiplying top area by depth overstates storage in an expanding basin. Omitted columns or initial water also inflate available capacity, and inconsistent datums can cause the same depth interval to be counted twice. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例採線性水位面積關係且從指定空池基準積分，未含柱體或死水容積；實際幾何需由測量和竣工資料建立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Actual geometry needs survey and as-built records.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「池頂平面面積乘總深度永遠等於可用滯洪容量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Top plan area times total depth always equals usable detention storage.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用頂面積乘深度會對向上擴張池體高估容積，漏掉柱體或既有積水也會虛增可用量；基準不一致時甚至可能把同一段水深重複計入。","textEn":"Multiplying top area by depth overstates storage in an expanding basin. Omitted columns or initial water also inflate available capacity, and inconsistent datums can cause the same depth interval to be counted twice.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「水位面積與有效池容機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Stage area and usable storage mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["用頂面積乘深度會對向上擴張池體高估容積，漏掉柱體或既有積水也會虛增可用量；基準不一致時甚至可能把同一段水深重複計入。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","孔口流量只和池內水深有關，下游水位升高不會影響。"],"optionsEn":["Multiplying top area by depth overstates storage in an expanding basin.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Orifice discharge depends only on basin depth and is unaffected by downstream water level."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用頂面積乘深度會對向上擴張池體高估容積，漏掉柱體或既有積水也會虛增可用量；基準不一致時甚至可能把同一段水深重複計入。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Multiplying top area by depth overstates storage in an expanding basin. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b271-v15-13","title":"孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「孔口出流與尾水」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Orifice release and tailwater” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"池底孔口把水頭轉為出流速度，流量取決於有效開口、流量係數及兩側能量差。自由出流時可由孔心到池水面估水頭，但下游淹沒後必須改用兩側水頭差；入口垃圾和沉積也會改變有效面積，不能把設計孔徑永久視為可用開口。本例是淹沒薄孔的簡化定常流，指定係數與兩側水頭差，忽略接管沿程損失；不推定任何產品或許可排量。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「孔口出流與尾水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A low-level orifice converts head to outlet velocity according to effective opening, discharge coefficient and energy difference. For free discharge the basin surface-to-orifice-center head may be used, but submerged discharge requires the difference between both sides. Debris and deposits alter effective area, so nominal diameter cannot be treated as permanently available opening. The example is simplified steady flow through a submerged thin orifice with specified coefficient and differential head, excluding downstream pipe friction and any product or permit rating. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Orifice release and tailwater” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Cd=0.62、開口A=0.10 m²、兩側水頭差ΔH=1.0 m、g=9.81 m/s²，Q=CdA√(2gΔH)=0.2746 m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Cd=0.62, opening A=0.10 m², differential head ΔH=1.0 m and g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「孔口流量只和池內水深有關，下游水位升高不會影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Orifice discharge depends only on basin depth and is unaffected by downstream water level.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「孔口出流與尾水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Orifice release and tailwater”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-13-k1","title":"孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證","titleEn":"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification","text":"池底孔口把水頭轉為出流速度，流量取決於有效開口、流量係數及兩側能量差。自由出流時可由孔心到池水面估水頭，但下游淹沒後必須改用兩側水頭差；入口垃圾和沉積也會改變有效面積，不能把設計孔徑永久視為可用開口。","textEn":"A low-level orifice converts head to outlet velocity according to effective opening, discharge coefficient and energy difference. For free discharge the basin surface-to-orifice-center head may be used, but submerged discharge requires the difference between both sides.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：孔口流量只和池內水深有關，下游水位升高不會影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Orifice discharge depends only on basin depth and is unaffected by downstream water level. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["孔口流量只和池內水深有關，下游水位升高不會影響。","池底孔口把水頭轉為出流速度，流量取決於有效開口、流量係數及兩側能量差。","只要設置溢流堰，超量洪水就已經有安全去處而不必追蹤。"],"optionsEn":["Orifice discharge depends only on basin depth and is unaffected by downstream water level.","A low-level orifice converts head to outlet velocity according to effective opening, discharge coefficient and energy difference.","An overflow weir automatically gives excess floodwater a safe destination without route analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"池底孔口把水頭轉為出流速度，流量取決於有效開口、流量係數及兩側能量差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A low-level orifice converts head to outlet velocity according to effective opening, discharge coefficient and energy difference. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b271-v15-14","title":"孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「孔口出流與尾水」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Orifice release and tailwater” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Cd=0.62、開口A=0.10 m²、兩側水頭差ΔH=1.0 m、g=9.81 m/s²，Q=CdA√(2gΔH)=0.2746 m³/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Cd=0.62, opening A=0.10 m², differential head ΔH=1.0 m and g=9.81 m/s². Flow Q=CdA√(2gΔH)=0.2746 m³/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同時量測池內與下游水位，核對孔心高程、開口和係數來源。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure basin and downstream stages together, checking orifice elevation, opening and coefficient source.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Cd=0.62、開口A=0.10 m²、兩側水頭差ΔH=1.0 m、g=9.81 m/s²，Q=CdA√(2gΔH)=0.2746 m³/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Cd=0.62, opening A=0.10 m², differential head ΔH=1.0 m and g=9.81 m/s². Flow Q=CdA√(2gΔH)=0.2746 m³/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["孔口排空時間可永遠用總水量除以一開始的最大出流量。","只要沉積占總池容比例很小，出口與滯洪效能就不可能受影響。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Cd=0.62、開口A=0.10 m²、兩側水頭差ΔH=1.0 m、g=9.81 m/s²，Q=CdA√(2gΔH)=0.2746 m³/s。"],"optionsEn":["Orifice drawdown time always equals total water volume divided by the initial maximum release.","A small deposited fraction of total storage cannot affect the outlet or detention performance.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Cd=0.62, opening A=0.10 m², differential head ΔH=1.0 m and g=9.81 m/s²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Cd=0.62、開口A=0.10 m²、兩側水頭差ΔH=1.0 m、g=9.81 m/s²，Q=CdA√(2gΔH)=0.2746 m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Cd=0.62, opening A=0.10 m², differential head ΔH=1.0 m and g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b271-v15-15","title":"孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「孔口出流與尾水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Orifice release and tailwater” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同時量測池內與下游水位，核對孔心高程、開口和係數來源。比較清潔、部分堵塞與尾水上升的出流資料，確認模型在自由與淹沒狀態切換時不會突然創造或消失流量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure basin and downstream stages together, checking orifice elevation, opening and coefficient source. Compare clean, partially blocked and rising-tailwater observations, ensuring that switching between free and submerged representations does not abruptly create or remove flow in the model. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：保持池水位不變而提高尾水，計算兩個水頭差的出流量。再將有效面積減半，區分堵塞和尾水兩種原因如何在量測上辨認。","observationEn":"Site practice: Hold basin stage fixed while raising tailwater and calculate releases at two differential heads. Then halve effective area, distinguishing the observations needed to separate blockage from a tailwater-driven reduction.","failure":"注意干擾：尾水升高仍用池深當水頭會高估出流而低估池水位，忽略堵塞則讓維護不足被掩蓋；水頭差反向時，未設防倒流的開口可能反而進水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using basin depth despite high tailwater overstates release and understates basin stage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同時量測池內與下游水位，核對孔心高程、開口和係數來源。比較清潔、部分堵塞與尾水上升的出流資料，確認模型在自由與淹沒狀態切換時不會突然創造或消失流量。","textEn":"Measure basin and downstream stages together, checking orifice elevation, opening and coefficient source. Compare clean, partially blocked and rising-tailwater observations, ensuring that switching between free and submerged representations does not abruptly create or remove flow in the model.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"保持池水位不變而提高尾水，計算兩個水頭差的出流量。再將有效面積減半，區分堵塞和尾水兩種原因如何在量測上辨認。","textEn":"Hold basin stage fixed while raising tailwater and calculate releases at two differential heads. Then halve effective area, distinguishing the observations needed to separate blockage from a tailwater-driven reduction.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification\"?","options":["同時量測池內與下游水位，核對孔心高程、開口和係數來源。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","知道總雨量與總面積後，就能唯一決定所需滯洪池容量。"],"optionsEn":["Measure basin and downstream stages together, checking orifice elevation, opening and coefficient source.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Total rainfall and total area uniquely determine the required detention capacity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同時量測池內與下游水位，核對孔心高程、開口和係數來源。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure basin and downstream stages together, checking orifice elevation, opening and coefficient source. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b271-v15-16","title":"孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「孔口出流與尾水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Orifice release and tailwater” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"尾水升高仍用池深當水頭會高估出流而低估池水位，忽略堵塞則讓維護不足被掩蓋；水頭差反向時，未設防倒流的開口可能反而進水。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using basin depth despite high tailwater overstates release and understates basin stage. Ignored blockage conceals maintenance loss, and reversed differential head can admit water through an opening without backflow protection. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例是淹沒薄孔的簡化定常流，指定係數與兩側水頭差，忽略接管沿程損失；不推定任何產品或許可排量。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The example is simplified steady flow through a submerged thin orifice with specified coefficient and differential head, excluding downstream pipe friction and any product or permit rating.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「孔口流量只和池內水深有關，下游水位升高不會影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Orifice discharge depends only on basin depth and is unaffected by downstream water level.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"尾水升高仍用池深當水頭會高估出流而低估池水位，忽略堵塞則讓維護不足被掩蓋；水頭差反向時，未設防倒流的開口可能反而進水。","textEn":"Using basin depth despite high tailwater overstates release and understates basin stage. Ignored blockage conceals maintenance loss, and reversed differential head can admit water through an opening without backflow protection.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「孔口出流與尾水機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Orifice release and tailwater mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","尾水升高仍用池深當水頭會高估出流而低估池水位，忽略堵塞則讓維護不足被掩蓋；水頭差反向時，未設防倒流的開口可能反而進水。","只要設置溢流堰，超量洪水就已經有安全去處而不必追蹤。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Using basin depth despite high tailwater overstates release and understates basin stage.","An overflow weir automatically gives excess floodwater a safe destination without route analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"尾水升高仍用池深當水頭會高估出流而低估池水位，忽略堵塞則讓維護不足被掩蓋；水頭差反向時，未設防倒流的開口可能反而進水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using basin depth despite high tailwater overstates release and understates basin stage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b271-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證」與「滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification\" and \"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b271-v15-17","title":"超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「超量溢流與越頂路徑」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Exceedance overflow and routes” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"滯洪池遇到超過控制出口能力的事件時，需要辨認水會流向何處，正常出流設計不能代表超量情境。溢流堰流量與堰頂以上水頭呈非線性，來流速度、淹沒與側向幾何會改變係數；更重要的是溢出後的路徑和受影響空間，不能只證明池內水位降低而忽略下游風險。本例用指定係數的自由矩形堰比較，係數已包含單位；未模擬側堰、淹沒或街道二維流動。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「超量溢流與越頂路徑」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"When an event exceeds the controlled outlet, the overflow destination matters; normal-release design does not represent exceedance behavior. Weir flow is nonlinear in head above crest, and approach velocity, submergence and lateral geometry alter the coefficient. The route and exposed spaces downstream must be assessed rather than claiming success merely because basin level is reduced. The example uses a free rectangular weir with a specified dimensional coefficient, excluding side-weir behavior, submergence and two-dimensional street flow. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Exceedance overflow and routes” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=Cw bH^1.5，Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s、堰寬b=2.0 m、水頭H=0.30 m，Q=0.5587 m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=Cw bH^1.5, Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s, width b=2.0 m and head H=0.30 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要設置溢流堰，超量洪水就已經有安全去處而不必追蹤。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An overflow weir automatically gives excess floodwater a safe destination without route analysis.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「超量溢流與越頂路徑」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Exceedance overflow and routes”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-17-k1","title":"超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證","titleEn":"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification","text":"滯洪池遇到超過控制出口能力的事件時，需要辨認水會流向何處，正常出流設計不能代表超量情境。溢流堰流量與堰頂以上水頭呈非線性，來流速度、淹沒與側向幾何會改變係數；更重要的是溢出後的路徑和受影響空間，不能只證明池內水位降低而忽略下游風險。","textEn":"When an event exceeds the controlled outlet, the overflow destination matters; normal-release design does not represent exceedance behavior. Weir flow is nonlinear in head above crest, and approach velocity, submergence and lateral geometry alter the coefficient.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要設置溢流堰，超量洪水就已經有安全去處而不必追蹤。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An overflow weir automatically gives excess floodwater a safe destination without route analysis. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["只要設置溢流堰，超量洪水就已經有安全去處而不必追蹤。","透水池底的入滲率永遠固定，因此可以無條件扣減所需池容。","滯洪池遇到超過控制出口能力的事件時，需要辨認水會流向何處，正常出流設計不能代表超量情境。"],"optionsEn":["An overflow weir automatically gives excess floodwater a safe destination without route analysis.","A permeable floor has constant infiltration that can always be deducted from required storage.","When an event exceeds the controlled outlet, the overflow destination matters; normal-release design does not represent exceedance behavior."],"answer":2,"explanation":"滯洪池遇到超過控制出口能力的事件時，需要辨認水會流向何處，正常出流設計不能代表超量情境。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"When an event exceeds the controlled outlet, the overflow destination matters; normal-release design does not represent exceedance behavior. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b271-v15-18","title":"超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「超量溢流與越頂路徑」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Exceedance overflow and routes” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=Cw bH^1.5，Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s、堰寬b=2.0 m、水頭H=0.30 m，Q=0.5587 m³/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=Cw bH^1.5, Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s, width b=2.0 m and head H=0.30 m. Overflow Q=0.5587 m³/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：測量堰頂、相鄰低點和下游路徑，核對流量係數及淹沒範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Survey crest, adjacent low points and downstream routes, checking coefficient basis and submergence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=Cw bH^1.5，Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s、堰寬b=2.0 m、水頭H=0.30 m，Q=0.5587 m³/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=Cw bH^1.5, Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s, width b=2.0 m and head H=0.30 m. Overflow Q=0.5587 m³/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=Cw bH^1.5，Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s、堰寬b=2.0 m、水頭H=0.30 m，Q=0.5587 m³/s。","每座滯洪池都降低自己的出口峰值，就能保證最下游峰值同比降低。","模型水量誤差很小，就等於峰值水位和所有設計判斷都正確。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=Cw bH^1.5, Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s, width b=2.0 m and head H=0.30 m.","Reducing each basin outlet peak guarantees the same proportional reduction at the downstream terminus.","A small model water-balance error proves correct peak stage and every design decision."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=Cw bH^1.5，Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s、堰寬b=2.0 m、水頭H=0.30 m，Q=0.5587 m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=Cw bH^1.5, Cw=1.70 m^0.5/s, width b=2.0 m and head H=0.30 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b271-v15-19","title":"超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「超量溢流與越頂路徑」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Exceedance overflow and routes” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"測量堰頂、相鄰低點和下游路徑，核對流量係數及淹沒範圍。以超量事件追蹤地面流向和深度，確認出口不導向脆弱空間，並保留正常出口堵塞時的獨立情境。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Survey crest, adjacent low points and downstream routes, checking coefficient basis and submergence. Track surface direction and depth during exceedance, verifying that overflow does not lead toward vulnerable spaces, and retain a separate scenario for blockage of the normal outlet. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：在地形圖標出設計溢流口和其他低點，為同一水位比較可能先出流的位置。用簡化堰式計算後，列出仍需地表流模型回答的深度與速度問題。","observationEn":"Site practice: Mark the designed overflow and other low points on a terrain map and compare which can spill first at one stage. After a weir calculation, identify depth and velocity questions still requiring surface-flow analysis.","failure":"注意干擾：把溢流量視為無害排出會漏掉街道或地下室的暴露，忽略鄰近較低缺口則可能使實際溢流繞過設計堰；下游回水還能降低溢流能力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating overflow as harmless removal overlooks street or basement exposure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"測量堰頂、相鄰低點和下游路徑，核對流量係數及淹沒範圍。以超量事件追蹤地面流向和深度，確認出口不導向脆弱空間，並保留正常出口堵塞時的獨立情境。","textEn":"Survey crest, adjacent low points and downstream routes, checking coefficient basis and submergence. Track surface direction and depth during exceedance, verifying that overflow does not lead toward vulnerable spaces, and retain a separate scenario for blockage of the normal outlet.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"在地形圖標出設計溢流口和其他低點，為同一水位比較可能先出流的位置。用簡化堰式計算後，列出仍需地表流模型回答的深度與速度問題。","textEn":"Mark the designed overflow and other low points on a terrain map and compare which can spill first at one stage. After a weir calculation, identify depth and velocity questions still requiring surface-flow analysis.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","測量堰頂、相鄰低點和下游路徑，核對流量係數及淹沒範圍。","所需滯洪容積就是最大入流減去最大出流，不需要積分時間。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Survey crest, adjacent low points and downstream routes, checking coefficient basis and submergence.","Required detention volume is maximum inflow minus maximum outflow without time integration."],"answer":1,"explanation":"測量堰頂、相鄰低點和下游路徑，核對流量係數及淹沒範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Survey crest, adjacent low points and downstream routes, checking coefficient basis and submergence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b271-v15-20","title":"超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「超量溢流與越頂路徑」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Exceedance overflow and routes” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把溢流量視為無害排出會漏掉街道或地下室的暴露，忽略鄰近較低缺口則可能使實際溢流繞過設計堰；下游回水還能降低溢流能力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating overflow as harmless removal overlooks street or basement exposure. A nearby lower gap may bypass the intended weir, and downstream backwater can further reduce the available overflow capacity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例用指定係數的自由矩形堰比較，係數已包含單位；未模擬側堰、淹沒或街道二維流動。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The example uses a free rectangular weir with a specified dimensional coefficient, excluding side-weir behavior, submergence and two-dimensional street flow.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要設置溢流堰，超量洪水就已經有安全去處而不必追蹤。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An overflow weir automatically gives excess floodwater a safe destination without route analysis.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把溢流量視為無害排出會漏掉街道或地下室的暴露，忽略鄰近較低缺口則可能使實際溢流繞過設計堰；下游回水還能降低溢流能力。","textEn":"Treating overflow as harmless removal overlooks street or basement exposure. A nearby lower gap may bypass the intended weir, and downstream backwater can further reduce the available overflow capacity.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「超量溢流與越頂路徑機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Exceedance overflow and routes mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","透水池底的入滲率永遠固定，因此可以無條件扣減所需池容。","把溢流量視為無害排出會漏掉街道或地下室的暴露，忽略鄰近較低缺口則可能使實際溢流繞過設計堰；下游回水還能降低溢流能力。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A permeable floor has constant infiltration that can always be deducted from required storage.","Treating overflow as harmless removal overlooks street or basement exposure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把溢流量視為無害排出會漏掉街道或地下室的暴露，忽略鄰近較低缺口則可能使實際溢流繞過設計堰；下游回水還能降低溢流能力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating overflow as harmless removal overlooks street or basement exposure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b271-v15-21","title":"滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「滲透折減與前期飽和」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"透水滯洪池可讓部分水進入地層，但滲透能力會受到前期含水、地下水位、細粒堵塞與土層連續性控制。短時間現地試驗不能直接代表長期暴雨條件，尤其地下水接近池底時，向下水力梯度可能減小；將滲透當作永遠固定的額外出口，可能低估連續降雨所需庫容。本例使用指定均勻入滲速率作體積尺度，沒有採用實測保證值；飽和、污染控制或襯底條件可能使可計入滲透為零。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「滲透折減與前期飽和」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A permeable basin can infiltrate some water, but antecedent wetness, groundwater, fine-particle clogging and stratigraphy control that capacity. A short field test does not necessarily represent prolonged rainfall, particularly when groundwater approaches the floor and downward gradient weakens. Treating infiltration as a permanently fixed extra outlet can understate storage needed during successive storms. The example uses a specified uniform infiltration rate as a volume scale, not a guaranteed field value. Saturation, contamination controls or lining may reduce creditable infiltration to zero. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設有效池底A=1000 m²、入滲率f=5 mm/h、時間t=2 h，滲透體積Vi=Aft=10.0 m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective floor A=1000 m², infiltration f=5 mm/h and duration t=2 h.","failure":"常見誤解：「透水池底的入滲率永遠固定，因此可以無條件扣減所需池容。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A permeable floor has constant infiltration that can always be deducted from required storage.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「滲透折減與前期飽和」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-21-k1","title":"滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證","titleEn":"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification","text":"透水滯洪池可讓部分水進入地層，但滲透能力會受到前期含水、地下水位、細粒堵塞與土層連續性控制。短時間現地試驗不能直接代表長期暴雨條件，尤其地下水接近池底時，向下水力梯度可能減小；將滲透當作永遠固定的額外出口，可能低估連續降雨所需庫容。","textEn":"A permeable basin can infiltrate some water, but antecedent wetness, groundwater, fine-particle clogging and stratigraphy control that capacity. A short field test does not necessarily represent prolonged rainfall, particularly when groundwater approaches the floor and downward gradient weakens.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：透水池底的入滲率永遠固定，因此可以無條件扣減所需池容。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A permeable floor has constant infiltration that can always be deducted from required storage. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["透水滯洪池可讓部分水進入地層，但滲透能力會受到前期含水、地下水位、細粒堵塞與土層連續性控制。","透水池底的入滲率永遠固定，因此可以無條件扣減所需池容。","孔口排空時間可永遠用總水量除以一開始的最大出流量。"],"optionsEn":["A permeable basin can infiltrate some water, but antecedent wetness, groundwater, fine-particle clogging and stratigraphy control that capacity.","A permeable floor has constant infiltration that can always be deducted from required storage.","Orifice drawdown time always equals total water volume divided by the initial maximum release."],"answer":0,"explanation":"透水滯洪池可讓部分水進入地層，但滲透能力會受到前期含水、地下水位、細粒堵塞與土層連續性控制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A permeable basin can infiltrate some water, but antecedent wetness, groundwater, fine-particle clogging and stratigraphy control that capacity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b271-v15-22","title":"滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「滲透折減與前期飽和」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設有效池底A=1000 m²、入滲率f=5 mm/h、時間t=2 h，滲透體積Vi=Aft=10.0 m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective floor A=1000 m², infiltration f=5 mm/h and duration t=2 h. Infiltrated volume Vi=Aft=10.0 m³. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在代表土層與季節進行入滲和地下水觀測，將試驗持續時間、前期含水與堵塞狀態記錄完整。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Observe infiltration and groundwater in representative strata and seasons, documenting test duration, antecedent wetness and clogging state.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設有效池底A=1000 m²、入滲率f=5 mm/h、時間t=2 h，滲透體積Vi=Aft=10.0 m³。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective floor A=1000 m², infiltration f=5 mm/h and duration t=2 h. Infiltrated volume Vi=Aft=10.0 m³.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["只要沉積占總池容比例很小，出口與滯洪效能就不可能受影響。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設有效池底A=1000 m²、入滲率f=5 mm/h、時間t=2 h，滲透體積Vi=Aft=10.0 m³。","知道總雨量與總面積後，就能唯一決定所需滯洪池容量。"],"optionsEn":["A small deposited fraction of total storage cannot affect the outlet or detention performance.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective floor A=1000 m², infiltration f=5 mm/h and duration t=2 h.","Total rainfall and total area uniquely determine the required detention capacity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設有效池底A=1000 m²、入滲率f=5 mm/h、時間t=2 h，滲透體積Vi=Aft=10.0 m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume effective floor A=1000 m², infiltration f=5 mm/h and duration t=2 h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b271-v15-23","title":"滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「滲透折減與前期飽和」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在代表土層與季節進行入滲和地下水觀測，將試驗持續時間、前期含水與堵塞狀態記錄完整。比較可計入與零滲透兩個情境，並確認水質或襯底需求不與假設滲透功能衝突。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Observe infiltration and groundwater in representative strata and seasons, documenting test duration, antecedent wetness and clogging state. Compare credited-infiltration and zero-infiltration cases, checking that water-quality or lining requirements do not contradict the infiltration function assumed by the storage model. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把指定滲透體積與事件逕流體積比較，判斷它在此假設下的相對影響。將入滲設為零重新演算，說明哪些場地證據才能支持恢復部分折減。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare the specified infiltration volume with event runoff to assess its relative influence under these assumptions. Rerun with zero infiltration and identify site evidence needed before restoring any infiltration credit.","failure":"注意干擾：以乾季初始入滲率外推連續暴雨會高估損失，孔隙堵塞又可能逐年降低能力；只計入滲優點而未檢查地下水與水質，會形成不完整的工程比較。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Extrapolating dry-season initial infiltration through prolonged storms overstates losses, while clogging can reduce performance over years. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在代表土層與季節進行入滲和地下水觀測，將試驗持續時間、前期含水與堵塞狀態記錄完整。比較可計入與零滲透兩個情境，並確認水質或襯底需求不與假設滲透功能衝突。","textEn":"Observe infiltration and groundwater in representative strata and seasons, documenting test duration, antecedent wetness and clogging state. Compare credited-infiltration and zero-infiltration cases, checking that water-quality or lining requirements do not contradict the infiltration function assumed by the storage model.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把指定滲透體積與事件逕流體積比較，判斷它在此假設下的相對影響。將入滲設為零重新演算，說明哪些場地證據才能支持恢復部分折減。","textEn":"Compare the specified infiltration volume with event runoff to assess its relative influence under these assumptions. Rerun with zero infiltration and identify site evidence needed before restoring any infiltration credit.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","池頂平面面積乘總深度永遠等於可用滯洪容量。","在代表土層與季節進行入滲和地下水觀測，將試驗持續時間、前期含水與堵塞狀態記錄完整。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Top plan area times total depth always equals usable detention storage.","Observe infiltration and groundwater in representative strata and seasons, documenting test duration, antecedent wetness and clogging state."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在代表土層與季節進行入滲和地下水觀測，將試驗持續時間、前期含水與堵塞狀態記錄完整。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Observe infiltration and groundwater in representative strata and seasons, documenting test duration, antecedent wetness and clogging state. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b271-v15-24","title":"滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「滲透折減與前期飽和」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以乾季初始入滲率外推連續暴雨會高估損失，孔隙堵塞又可能逐年降低能力；只計入滲優點而未檢查地下水與水質，會形成不完整的工程比較。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Extrapolating dry-season initial infiltration through prolonged storms overstates losses, while clogging can reduce performance over years. Counting infiltration benefits without groundwater and water-quality checks produces an incomplete engineering comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例使用指定均勻入滲速率作體積尺度，沒有採用實測保證值；飽和、污染控制或襯底條件可能使可計入滲透為零。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Saturation, contamination controls or lining may reduce creditable infiltration to zero.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「透水池底的入滲率永遠固定，因此可以無條件扣減所需池容。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A permeable floor has constant infiltration that can always be deducted from required storage.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以乾季初始入滲率外推連續暴雨會高估損失，孔隙堵塞又可能逐年降低能力；只計入滲優點而未檢查地下水與水質，會形成不完整的工程比較。","textEn":"Extrapolating dry-season initial infiltration through prolonged storms overstates losses, while clogging can reduce performance over years. Counting infiltration benefits without groundwater and water-quality checks produces an incomplete engineering comparison.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「滲透折減與前期飽和機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Infiltration credit and antecedent saturation mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["以乾季初始入滲率外推連續暴雨會高估損失，孔隙堵塞又可能逐年降低能力；只計入滲優點而未檢查地下水與水質，會形成不完整的工程比較。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","孔口排空時間可永遠用總水量除以一開始的最大出流量。"],"optionsEn":["Extrapolating dry-season initial infiltration through prolonged storms overstates losses, while clogging can reduce performance over years.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Orifice drawdown time always equals total water volume divided by the initial maximum release."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以乾季初始入滲率外推連續暴雨會高估損失，孔隙堵塞又可能逐年降低能力；只計入滲優點而未檢查地下水與水質，會形成不完整的工程比較。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Extrapolating dry-season initial infiltration through prolonged storms overstates losses, while clogging can reduce performance over years. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b271-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「變水頭排空時間機理與驗證」與「下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification\" and \"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b271-v15-25","title":"變水頭排空時間機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「變水頭排空時間」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Drawdown under changing head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"孔口排水會隨水位下降而減慢，因此以初始最大出流除池容會低估排空時間。若後續降雨在池尚未恢復容量時到達，前一場殘留水會改變下一場峰值；排空策略需同時考慮下游容許出流和連續事件，而非只追求單場暴雨結束後最快放空。本例池面積固定、無入流與滲透、自由孔口小到可用孔心水頭近似，積分到仍為正的水頭；不外推到孔口部分露出階段。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「變水頭排空時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Orifice release slows as stage falls, so dividing storage by the initial maximum discharge understates drawdown time. A second storm arriving before recovery encounters less available storage. Drawdown planning must therefore consider downstream release constraints and successive events rather than simply emptying as quickly as possible after one storm. The example assumes constant basin area, no inflow or infiltration and a small free orifice described by center head, integrating only to a positive head before partial uncovering. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drawdown under changing head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池面積Ab=1000 m²、Cd=0.62、孔面a=0.10 m²、h1=2.0、h2=0.20 m，t=2Ab(√h1−√h2)/(Cd a√(2g))=7042 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume basin Ab=1000 m², Cd=0.62, orifice a=0.10 m², h1=2.0, h2=0.20 m and g=9.81 m/s².","failure":"常見誤解：「孔口排空時間可永遠用總水量除以一開始的最大出流量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Orifice drawdown time always equals total water volume divided by the initial maximum release.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「變水頭排空時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drawdown under changing head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-25-k1","title":"變水頭排空時間機理與驗證","titleEn":"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification","text":"孔口排水會隨水位下降而減慢，因此以初始最大出流除池容會低估排空時間。若後續降雨在池尚未恢復容量時到達，前一場殘留水會改變下一場峰值；排空策略需同時考慮下游容許出流和連續事件，而非只追求單場暴雨結束後最快放空。","textEn":"Orifice release slows as stage falls, so dividing storage by the initial maximum discharge understates drawdown time. A second storm arriving before recovery encounters less available storage.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：孔口排空時間可永遠用總水量除以一開始的最大出流量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Orifice drawdown time always equals total water volume divided by the initial maximum release. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「變水頭排空時間機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["孔口排空時間可永遠用總水量除以一開始的最大出流量。","孔口排水會隨水位下降而減慢，因此以初始最大出流除池容會低估排空時間。","每座滯洪池都降低自己的出口峰值，就能保證最下游峰值同比降低。"],"optionsEn":["Orifice drawdown time always equals total water volume divided by the initial maximum release.","Orifice release slows as stage falls, so dividing storage by the initial maximum discharge understates drawdown time.","Reducing each basin outlet peak guarantees the same proportional reduction at the downstream terminus."],"answer":1,"explanation":"孔口排水會隨水位下降而減慢，因此以初始最大出流除池容會低估排空時間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Orifice release slows as stage falls, so dividing storage by the initial maximum discharge understates drawdown time. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b271-v15-26","title":"變水頭排空時間機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「變水頭排空時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Drawdown under changing head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池面積Ab=1000 m²、Cd=0.62、孔面a=0.10 m²、h1=2.0、h2=0.20 m，t=2Ab(√h1−√h2)/(Cd a√(2g))=7042 s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume basin Ab=1000 m², Cd=0.62, orifice a=0.10 m², h1=2.0, h2=0.20 m and g=9.81 m/s². Drawdown t=7042 s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用不同水位下實測出流檢查孔口關係，核對排空期間是否仍有管網入流或尾水抬升。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check the outlet relation using measured releases at several stages and identify continuing network inflow or rising tailwater during drawdown.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池面積Ab=1000 m²、Cd=0.62、孔面a=0.10 m²、h1=2.0、h2=0.20 m，t=2Ab(√h1−√h2)/(Cd a√(2g))=7042 s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume basin Ab=1000 m², Cd=0.62, orifice a=0.10 m², h1=2.0, h2=0.20 m and g=9.81 m/s². Drawdown t=7042 s.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「變水頭排空時間機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["模型水量誤差很小，就等於峰值水位和所有設計判斷都正確。","所需滯洪容積就是最大入流減去最大出流，不需要積分時間。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池面積Ab=1000 m²、Cd=0.62、孔面a=0.10 m²、h1=2.0、h2=0.20 m，t=2Ab(√h1−√h2)/(Cd a√(2g))=7042 s。"],"optionsEn":["A small model water-balance error proves correct peak stage and every design decision.","Required detention volume is maximum inflow minus maximum outflow without time integration.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume basin Ab=1000 m², Cd=0.62, orifice a=0.10 m², h1=2.0, h2=0.20 m and g=9.81 m/s²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池面積Ab=1000 m²、Cd=0.62、孔面a=0.10 m²、h1=2.0、h2=0.20 m，t=2Ab(√h1−√h2)/(Cd a√(2g))=7042 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume basin Ab=1000 m², Cd=0.62, orifice a=0.10 m², h1=2.0, h2=0.20 m and g=9.81 m/s². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b271-v15-27","title":"變水頭排空時間機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「變水頭排空時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Drawdown under changing head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用不同水位下實測出流檢查孔口關係，核對排空期間是否仍有管網入流或尾水抬升。比較積分解與逐步演算，並確認終止水頭仍符合孔口完整淹沒的幾何假設。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check the outlet relation using measured releases at several stages and identify continuing network inflow or rising tailwater during drawdown. Compare the integrated solution with stepwise routing, verifying that the final head still satisfies the assumed geometry of a fully covered opening. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較固定初始流量估計與變水頭積分結果，畫出排水逐漸減慢的曲線。讓第二場雨在恢復前到達，指出演算必須保留的初始儲量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare a fixed-initial-flow estimate with changing-head integration and plot the slowing release. Introduce a second storm before recovery and identify the initial storage that must carry into the new routing calculation.","failure":"注意干擾：以初始流量當全程固定會低估恢復容量所需時間，忽略尾水或再降雨更會過度樂觀；積分到孔口露出後仍沿用同式，則超出原有流況。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Holding the initial discharge constant understates recovery time, and omitted tailwater or renewed rainfall makes it more optimistic. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用不同水位下實測出流檢查孔口關係，核對排空期間是否仍有管網入流或尾水抬升。比較積分解與逐步演算，並確認終止水頭仍符合孔口完整淹沒的幾何假設。","textEn":"Check the outlet relation using measured releases at several stages and identify continuing network inflow or rising tailwater during drawdown. Compare the integrated solution with stepwise routing, verifying that the final head still satisfies the assumed geometry of a fully covered opening.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較固定初始流量估計與變水頭積分結果，畫出排水逐漸減慢的曲線。讓第二場雨在恢復前到達，指出演算必須保留的初始儲量。","textEn":"Compare a fixed-initial-flow estimate with changing-head integration and plot the slowing release. Introduce a second storm before recovery and identify the initial storage that must carry into the new routing calculation.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「變水頭排空時間機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification\"?","options":["用不同水位下實測出流檢查孔口關係，核對排空期間是否仍有管網入流或尾水抬升。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","孔口流量只和池內水深有關，下游水位升高不會影響。"],"optionsEn":["Check the outlet relation using measured releases at several stages and identify continuing network inflow or rising tailwater during drawdown.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Orifice discharge depends only on basin depth and is unaffected by downstream water level."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用不同水位下實測出流檢查孔口關係，核對排空期間是否仍有管網入流或尾水抬升。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check the outlet relation using measured releases at several stages and identify continuing network inflow or rising tailwater during drawdown. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b271-v15-28","title":"變水頭排空時間機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「變水頭排空時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Drawdown under changing head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以初始流量當全程固定會低估恢復容量所需時間，忽略尾水或再降雨更會過度樂觀；積分到孔口露出後仍沿用同式，則超出原有流況。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Holding the initial discharge constant understates recovery time, and omitted tailwater or renewed rainfall makes it more optimistic. Continuing the same equation after the opening becomes exposed extends it beyond the assumed flow regime. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例池面積固定、無入流與滲透、自由孔口小到可用孔心水頭近似，積分到仍為正的水頭；不外推到孔口部分露出階段。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The example assumes constant basin area, no inflow or infiltration and a small free orifice described by center head, integrating only to a positive head before partial uncovering.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「孔口排空時間可永遠用總水量除以一開始的最大出流量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Orifice drawdown time always equals total water volume divided by the initial maximum release.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以初始流量當全程固定會低估恢復容量所需時間，忽略尾水或再降雨更會過度樂觀；積分到孔口露出後仍沿用同式，則超出原有流況。","textEn":"Holding the initial discharge constant understates recovery time, and omitted tailwater or renewed rainfall makes it more optimistic. Continuing the same equation after the opening becomes exposed extends it beyond the assumed flow regime.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「變水頭排空時間機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Drawdown under changing head mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","以初始流量當全程固定會低估恢復容量所需時間，忽略尾水或再降雨更會過度樂觀；積分到孔口露出後仍沿用同式，則超出原有流況。","每座滯洪池都降低自己的出口峰值，就能保證最下游峰值同比降低。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Holding the initial discharge constant understates recovery time, and omitted tailwater or renewed rainfall makes it more optimistic.","Reducing each basin outlet peak guarantees the same proportional reduction at the downstream terminus."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以初始流量當全程固定會低估恢復容量所需時間，忽略尾水或再降雨更會過度樂觀；積分到孔口露出後仍沿用同式，則超出原有流況。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Holding the initial discharge constant understates recovery time, and omitted tailwater or renewed rainfall makes it more optimistic. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b271-v15-29","title":"下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「下游匯流與峰值錯時」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Downstream combination and peak timing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"單一池出口削峰不一定降低流域最下游峰值，因延後的出流可能剛好與另一支流洪峰重疊。配置池址和出流歷線時應在共同時間軸上做河網演算，不能把各支流最大值不加區分地相加；也不能只比較工程前後同一個時刻而忽略新峰值出現時間。本例在匯流點忽略傳播延遲與局部儲水，只示範同時流量相加；完整流域需先把各歷線演算至同一位置。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「下游匯流與峰值錯時」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Attenuation at one basin outlet does not necessarily reduce the furthest downstream peak: delayed release may coincide with another tributary crest. Basin siting and release hydrographs require routing on a shared time axis. Adding separate maxima ignores timing, while comparing only one preselected instant can miss a new peak occurring later. The example neglects travel time and local storage at a junction and demonstrates only simultaneous addition. Full-basin work must route each hydrograph to the same location first. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Downstream combination and peak timing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩支流在時刻t1為8與2 m³/s、t2為3與7 m³/s，兩時刻合流皆10 m³/s；各自峰值相加15 m³/s並非同時峰值。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume tributaries are 8 and 2 m³/s at t1, then 3 and 7 m³/s at t2.","failure":"常見誤解：「每座滯洪池都降低自己的出口峰值，就能保證最下游峰值同比降低。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Reducing each basin outlet peak guarantees the same proportional reduction at the downstream terminus.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「下游匯流與峰值錯時」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Downstream combination and peak timing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-29-k1","title":"下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證","titleEn":"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification","text":"單一池出口削峰不一定降低流域最下游峰值，因延後的出流可能剛好與另一支流洪峰重疊。配置池址和出流歷線時應在共同時間軸上做河網演算，不能把各支流最大值不加區分地相加；也不能只比較工程前後同一個時刻而忽略新峰值出現時間。","textEn":"Attenuation at one basin outlet does not necessarily reduce the furthest downstream peak: delayed release may coincide with another tributary crest. Basin siting and release hydrographs require routing on a shared time axis.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每座滯洪池都降低自己的出口峰值，就能保證最下游峰值同比降低。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Reducing each basin outlet peak guarantees the same proportional reduction at the downstream terminus. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["每座滯洪池都降低自己的出口峰值，就能保證最下游峰值同比降低。","只要沉積占總池容比例很小，出口與滯洪效能就不可能受影響。","單一池出口削峰不一定降低流域最下游峰值，因延後的出流可能剛好與另一支流洪峰重疊。"],"optionsEn":["Reducing each basin outlet peak guarantees the same proportional reduction at the downstream terminus.","A small deposited fraction of total storage cannot affect the outlet or detention performance.","Attenuation at one basin outlet does not necessarily reduce the furthest downstream peak: delayed release may coincide with another tributary crest."],"answer":2,"explanation":"單一池出口削峰不一定降低流域最下游峰值，因延後的出流可能剛好與另一支流洪峰重疊。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Attenuation at one basin outlet does not necessarily reduce the furthest downstream peak: delayed release may coincide with another tributary crest. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b271-v15-30","title":"下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「下游匯流與峰值錯時」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Downstream combination and peak timing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩支流在時刻t1為8與2 m³/s、t2為3與7 m³/s，兩時刻合流皆10 m³/s；各自峰值相加15 m³/s並非同時峰值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume tributaries are 8 and 2 m³/s at t1, then 3 and 7 m³/s at t2. Both totals are 10 m³/s; adding separate peaks gives 15 m³/s without concurrence. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將各支流與池出口時間戳統一並校核傳播時間，在匯流點比較完整工程前後歷線。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align tributary and basin-outlet timestamps and verify travel times before comparing complete pre- and post-project hydrographs at the junction.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩支流在時刻t1為8與2 m³/s、t2為3與7 m³/s，兩時刻合流皆10 m³/s；各自峰值相加15 m³/s並非同時峰值。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume tributaries are 8 and 2 m³/s at t1, then 3 and 7 m³/s at t2. Both totals are 10 m³/s; adding separate peaks gives 15 m³/s without concurrence.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩支流在時刻t1為8與2 m³/s、t2為3與7 m³/s，兩時刻合流皆10 m³/s。","知道總雨量與總面積後，就能唯一決定所需滯洪池容量。","池頂平面面積乘總深度永遠等於可用滯洪容量。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume tributaries are 8 and 2 m³/s at t1, then 3 and 7 m³/s at t2.","Total rainfall and total area uniquely determine the required detention capacity.","Top plan area times total depth always equals usable detention storage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設兩支流在時刻t1為8與2 m³/s、t2為3與7 m³/s，兩時刻合流皆10 m³/s；各自峰值相加15 m³/s並非同時峰值。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume tributaries are 8 and 2 m³/s at t1, then 3 and 7 m³/s at t2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b271-v15-31","title":"下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「下游匯流與峰值錯時」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Downstream combination and peak timing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將各支流與池出口時間戳統一並校核傳播時間，在匯流點比較完整工程前後歷線。檢查峰值時刻、持續時間及受納水位，而不是只記錄池出口的單一削峰百分比。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align tributary and basin-outlet timestamps and verify travel times before comparing complete pre- and post-project hydrographs at the junction. Examine crest timing, duration and receiving stage instead of reporting only one attenuation percentage measured at the basin outlet. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：把一支出流歷線平移一個時間步，重新計算匯流而不改總體積。比較局部峰值和下游峰值，說明時間配置為何是池址規劃的一部分。","observationEn":"Site practice: Shift one release hydrograph by one step without changing volume and recompute junction flow. Compare local and downstream peaks, explaining why temporal alignment is part of basin planning rather than a secondary plotting detail.","failure":"注意干擾：延遲出流若與另一支流同時達峰，可能把局部改善轉成下游負擔；直接加各峰值會高估某些情境，但忽略時間變化也可能漏掉真正最不利組合。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Delayed release can coincide with another tributary crest and transfer a local improvement downstream. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將各支流與池出口時間戳統一並校核傳播時間，在匯流點比較完整工程前後歷線。檢查峰值時刻、持續時間及受納水位，而不是只記錄池出口的單一削峰百分比。","textEn":"Align tributary and basin-outlet timestamps and verify travel times before comparing complete pre- and post-project hydrographs at the junction. Examine crest timing, duration and receiving stage instead of reporting only one attenuation percentage measured at the basin outlet.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"把一支出流歷線平移一個時間步，重新計算匯流而不改總體積。比較局部峰值和下游峰值，說明時間配置為何是池址規劃的一部分。","textEn":"Shift one release hydrograph by one step without changing volume and recompute junction flow. Compare local and downstream peaks, explaining why temporal alignment is part of basin planning rather than a secondary plotting detail.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將各支流與池出口時間戳統一並校核傳播時間，在匯流點比較完整工程前後歷線。","只要設置溢流堰，超量洪水就已經有安全去處而不必追蹤。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Align tributary and basin-outlet timestamps and verify travel times before comparing complete pre- and post-project hydrographs at the junction.","An overflow weir automatically gives excess floodwater a safe destination without route analysis."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將各支流與池出口時間戳統一並校核傳播時間，在匯流點比較完整工程前後歷線。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align tributary and basin-outlet timestamps and verify travel times before comparing complete pre- and post-project hydrographs at the junction. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b271-v15-32","title":"下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「下游匯流與峰值錯時」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Downstream combination and peak timing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"延遲出流若與另一支流同時達峰，可能把局部改善轉成下游負擔；直接加各峰值會高估某些情境，但忽略時間變化也可能漏掉真正最不利組合。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Delayed release can coincide with another tributary crest and transfer a local improvement downstream. Adding separate maxima overstates some scenarios, but ignoring changing timing can also miss the truly unfavorable combination. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例在匯流點忽略傳播延遲與局部儲水，只示範同時流量相加；完整流域需先把各歷線演算至同一位置。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Full-basin work must route each hydrograph to the same location first.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每座滯洪池都降低自己的出口峰值，就能保證最下游峰值同比降低。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reducing each basin outlet peak guarantees the same proportional reduction at the downstream terminus.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"延遲出流若與另一支流同時達峰，可能把局部改善轉成下游負擔；直接加各峰值會高估某些情境，但忽略時間變化也可能漏掉真正最不利組合。","textEn":"Delayed release can coincide with another tributary crest and transfer a local improvement downstream. Adding separate maxima overstates some scenarios, but ignoring changing timing can also miss the truly unfavorable combination.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「下游匯流與峰值錯時機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Downstream combination and peak timing mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要沉積占總池容比例很小，出口與滯洪效能就不可能受影響。","延遲出流若與另一支流同時達峰，可能把局部改善轉成下游負擔；直接加各峰值會高估某些情境，但忽略時間變化也可能漏掉真正最不利組合。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A small deposited fraction of total storage cannot affect the outlet or detention performance.","Delayed release can coincide with another tributary crest and transfer a local improvement downstream."],"answer":2,"explanation":"延遲出流若與另一支流同時達峰，可能把局部改善轉成下游負擔；直接加各峰值會高估某些情境，但忽略時間變化也可能漏掉真正最不利組合。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Delayed release can coincide with another tributary crest and transfer a local improvement downstream. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b271-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證」與「數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification\" and \"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b271-v15-33","title":"沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「沉積與可用容量維持」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Sediment and retained capacity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"滯洪池會接收顆粒與垃圾，沉積不僅占去容積，也可能堵塞出口或改變入流分配。總容量衰減與局部水力失效是不同路徑，平均薄層估算不能代表出口附近的堆積；維護應以測量、出流能力和可清理性共同評估，而不是等到池完全填滿才處理。本例沉積層厚度均勻且直接扣除有效容積，未模擬固結或出流堵塞；真實局部影響可能比體積比例更早主導。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沉積與可用容量維持」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Detention basins receive particles and debris that occupy volume, obstruct outlets and redistribute incoming flow. Bulk storage loss and localized hydraulic failure are different mechanisms, and a mean thin-layer estimate does not represent deposits near an outlet. Maintenance should combine survey, outlet performance and cleaning access rather than wait until the entire basin fills. The example subtracts a uniform deposit layer from usable storage without consolidation or outlet blockage. Local hydraulic effects may govern before the bulk volume fraction becomes large. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sediment and retained capacity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池底A=1000 m²、平均沉積厚度d=0.15 m，損失Vd=Ad=150 m³；原可用2400 m³剩2250 m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume floor A=1000 m² and mean deposit thickness d=0.15 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要沉積占總池容比例很小，出口與滯洪效能就不可能受影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A small deposited fraction of total storage cannot affect the outlet or detention performance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沉積與可用容量維持」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sediment and retained capacity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-33-k1","title":"沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證","titleEn":"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification","text":"滯洪池會接收顆粒與垃圾，沉積不僅占去容積，也可能堵塞出口或改變入流分配。總容量衰減與局部水力失效是不同路徑，平均薄層估算不能代表出口附近的堆積；維護應以測量、出流能力和可清理性共同評估，而不是等到池完全填滿才處理。","textEn":"Detention basins receive particles and debris that occupy volume, obstruct outlets and redistribute incoming flow. Bulk storage loss and localized hydraulic failure are different mechanisms, and a mean thin-layer estimate does not represent deposits near an outlet.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要沉積占總池容比例很小，出口與滯洪效能就不可能受影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A small deposited fraction of total storage cannot affect the outlet or detention performance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["滯洪池會接收顆粒與垃圾，沉積不僅占去容積，也可能堵塞出口或改變入流分配。","只要沉積占總池容比例很小，出口與滯洪效能就不可能受影響。","模型水量誤差很小，就等於峰值水位和所有設計判斷都正確。"],"optionsEn":["Detention basins receive particles and debris that occupy volume, obstruct outlets and redistribute incoming flow.","A small deposited fraction of total storage cannot affect the outlet or detention performance.","A small model water-balance error proves correct peak stage and every design decision."],"answer":0,"explanation":"滯洪池會接收顆粒與垃圾，沉積不僅占去容積，也可能堵塞出口或改變入流分配。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Detention basins receive particles and debris that occupy volume, obstruct outlets and redistribute incoming flow. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b271-v15-34","title":"沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沉積與可用容量維持」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Sediment and retained capacity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池底A=1000 m²、平均沉積厚度d=0.15 m，損失Vd=Ad=150 m³；原可用2400 m³剩2250 m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume floor A=1000 m² and mean deposit thickness d=0.15 m. Lost Vd=Ad=150 m³; initial usable 2400 m³ becomes 2250 m³. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以固定基準測深並標出出口附近的局部堆積，將清淤量與容積曲線更新對帳。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Survey deposits on a fixed datum and map local buildup near the outlet, reconciling removed volume with the updated storage curve.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池底A=1000 m²、平均沉積厚度d=0.15 m，損失Vd=Ad=150 m³；原可用2400 m³剩2250 m³。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume floor A=1000 m² and mean deposit thickness d=0.15 m. Lost Vd=Ad=150 m³; initial usable 2400 m³ becomes 2250 m³.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["所需滯洪容積就是最大入流減去最大出流，不需要積分時間。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池底A=1000 m²、平均沉積厚度d=0.15 m，損失Vd=Ad=150 m³。","孔口流量只和池內水深有關，下游水位升高不會影響。"],"optionsEn":["Required detention volume is maximum inflow minus maximum outflow without time integration.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume floor A=1000 m² and mean deposit thickness d=0.15 m.","Orifice discharge depends only on basin depth and is unaffected by downstream water level."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設池底A=1000 m²、平均沉積厚度d=0.15 m，損失Vd=Ad=150 m³；原可用2400 m³剩2250 m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume floor A=1000 m² and mean deposit thickness d=0.15 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b271-v15-35","title":"沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沉積與可用容量維持」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sediment and retained capacity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以固定基準測深並標出出口附近的局部堆積，將清淤量與容積曲線更新對帳。另測正常出口能力及垃圾攔截狀態，確認容量恢復和水力通暢都已驗證而非只完成清理作業。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Survey deposits on a fixed datum and map local buildup near the outlet, reconciling removed volume with the updated storage curve. Independently check normal-release capacity and debris control so that both recovered storage and hydraulic openness are verified, not merely the completion of cleaning work. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較均勻沉積和集中堵住孔口兩種同體積情境，分別更新池容與出流關係。說明為何維護績效需要容量和水力兩個指標，而不是只報清出重量。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare uniform deposition with the same volume concentrated at the orifice, updating storage and release relations separately. Explain why maintenance performance needs both capacity and hydraulic indicators rather than only removed mass.","failure":"注意干擾：只扣平均沉積容積會漏掉孔口先被堵塞的情況，未更新模型則持續高估可用池容；清淤若只移動泥砂到另一區，也不代表總有效容量已恢復。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Subtracting mean deposit volume misses an outlet blocked first, while an unchanged model continues to overstate storage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以固定基準測深並標出出口附近的局部堆積，將清淤量與容積曲線更新對帳。另測正常出口能力及垃圾攔截狀態，確認容量恢復和水力通暢都已驗證而非只完成清理作業。","textEn":"Survey deposits on a fixed datum and map local buildup near the outlet, reconciling removed volume with the updated storage curve. Independently check normal-release capacity and debris control so that both recovered storage and hydraulic openness are verified, not merely the completion of cleaning work.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較均勻沉積和集中堵住孔口兩種同體積情境，分別更新池容與出流關係。說明為何維護績效需要容量和水力兩個指標，而不是只報清出重量。","textEn":"Compare uniform deposition with the same volume concentrated at the orifice, updating storage and release relations separately. Explain why maintenance performance needs both capacity and hydraulic indicators rather than only removed mass.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","透水池底的入滲率永遠固定，因此可以無條件扣減所需池容。","以固定基準測深並標出出口附近的局部堆積，將清淤量與容積曲線更新對帳。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A permeable floor has constant infiltration that can always be deducted from required storage.","Survey deposits on a fixed datum and map local buildup near the outlet, reconciling removed volume with the updated storage curve."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以固定基準測深並標出出口附近的局部堆積，將清淤量與容積曲線更新對帳。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Survey deposits on a fixed datum and map local buildup near the outlet, reconciling removed volume with the updated storage curve. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b271-v15-36","title":"沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沉積與可用容量維持」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sediment and retained capacity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只扣平均沉積容積會漏掉孔口先被堵塞的情況，未更新模型則持續高估可用池容；清淤若只移動泥砂到另一區，也不代表總有效容量已恢復。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Subtracting mean deposit volume misses an outlet blocked first, while an unchanged model continues to overstate storage. Moving sediment to another part of the basin does not necessarily restore total usable capacity. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例沉積層厚度均勻且直接扣除有效容積，未模擬固結或出流堵塞；真實局部影響可能比體積比例更早主導。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Local hydraulic effects may govern before the bulk volume fraction becomes large.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要沉積占總池容比例很小，出口與滯洪效能就不可能受影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A small deposited fraction of total storage cannot affect the outlet or detention performance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只扣平均沉積容積會漏掉孔口先被堵塞的情況，未更新模型則持續高估可用池容；清淤若只移動泥砂到另一區，也不代表總有效容量已恢復。","textEn":"Subtracting mean deposit volume misses an outlet blocked first, while an unchanged model continues to overstate storage. Moving sediment to another part of the basin does not necessarily restore total usable capacity.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沉積與可用容量維持機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Sediment and retained capacity mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只扣平均沉積容積會漏掉孔口先被堵塞的情況，未更新模型則持續高估可用池容；清淤若只移動泥砂到另一區，也不代表總有效容量已恢復。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","模型水量誤差很小，就等於峰值水位和所有設計判斷都正確。"],"optionsEn":["Subtracting mean deposit volume misses an outlet blocked first, while an unchanged model continues to overstate storage.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A small model water-balance error proves correct peak stage and every design decision."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只扣平均沉積容積會漏掉孔口先被堵塞的情況，未更新模型則持續高估可用池容；清淤若只移動泥砂到另一區，也不代表總有效容量已恢復。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Subtracting mean deposit volume misses an outlet blocked first, while an unchanged model continues to overstate storage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b271-v15-37","title":"數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「數值水量閉合與收斂」如何影響都市滯洪池配置的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Numerical closure and convergence” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Urban detention-basin planning”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"雨洪模型的水量閉合檢查能發現漏列出流、時間積分或邊界處理問題，但閉合良好不代表洪峰位置或水位一定正確。粗網格和粗時間步可能保住總體積卻錯過短時高水位，錯誤糙率也能得到漂亮收支；因此守恆、時間收斂與獨立事件驗證應分開進行。本例殘差定義為入流減出流再減儲量增加，百分比以總入流作分母；正殘差只表示未解釋水量，並不直接指出物理漏水位置。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「數值水量閉合與收斂」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A water-balance check can reveal missing outlets, integration problems or boundary errors, but good closure does not prove correct peak timing or stage. Coarse grids and time steps can preserve volume while missing brief high water, and wrong roughness may still yield a neat balance. Conservation, temporal convergence and independent-event validation therefore require separate checks. Residual is inflow minus outflow minus storage increase, normalized by total inflow. A positive residual is unexplained water and does not locate a physical leak. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Numerical closure and convergence” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件入流Vi=10000 m³、出流Vo=7600 m³、儲量增ΔS=2350 m³，殘差R=50 m³，即入流的0.50%。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event inflow Vi=10000 m³, outflow Vo=7600 m³ and storage increase ΔS=2350 m³.","failure":"常見誤解：「模型水量誤差很小，就等於峰值水位和所有設計判斷都正確。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A small model water-balance error proves correct peak stage and every design decision.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「數值水量閉合與收斂」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Numerical closure and convergence”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-37-k1","title":"數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證","titleEn":"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification","text":"雨洪模型的水量閉合檢查能發現漏列出流、時間積分或邊界處理問題，但閉合良好不代表洪峰位置或水位一定正確。粗網格和粗時間步可能保住總體積卻錯過短時高水位，錯誤糙率也能得到漂亮收支；因此守恆、時間收斂與獨立事件驗證應分開進行。","textEn":"A water-balance check can reveal missing outlets, integration problems or boundary errors, but good closure does not prove correct peak timing or stage. Coarse grids and time steps can preserve volume while missing brief high water, and wrong roughness may still yield a neat balance.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：模型水量誤差很小，就等於峰值水位和所有設計判斷都正確。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A small model water-balance error proves correct peak stage and every design decision. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["模型水量誤差很小，就等於峰值水位和所有設計判斷都正確。","雨洪模型的水量閉合檢查能發現漏列出流、時間積分或邊界處理問題，但閉合良好不代表洪峰位置或水位一定正確。","知道總雨量與總面積後，就能唯一決定所需滯洪池容量。"],"optionsEn":["A small model water-balance error proves correct peak stage and every design decision.","A water-balance check can reveal missing outlets, integration problems or boundary errors, but good closure does not prove correct peak timing or stage.","Total rainfall and total area uniquely determine the required detention capacity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"雨洪模型的水量閉合檢查能發現漏列出流、時間積分或邊界處理問題，但閉合良好不代表洪峰位置或水位一定正確。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A water-balance check can reveal missing outlets, integration problems or boundary errors, but good closure does not prove correct peak timing or stage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b271-v15-38","title":"數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「數值水量閉合與收斂」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Numerical closure and convergence” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件入流Vi=10000 m³、出流Vo=7600 m³、儲量增ΔS=2350 m³，殘差R=50 m³，即入流的0.50%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event inflow Vi=10000 m³, outflow Vo=7600 m³ and storage increase ΔS=2350 m³. Residual R=50 m³, or 0.50% of inflow. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：列出所有水量項與正負號，核對初始儲量、溢流、滲透和反向流是否都有計入。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: List all terms with signs, checking initial storage, overflow, infiltration and reversed flow.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件入流Vi=10000 m³、出流Vo=7600 m³、儲量增ΔS=2350 m³，殘差R=50 m³，即入流的0.50%。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event inflow Vi=10000 m³, outflow Vo=7600 m³ and storage increase ΔS=2350 m³. Residual R=50 m³, or 0.50% of inflow.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["池頂平面面積乘總深度永遠等於可用滯洪容量。","只要設置溢流堰，超量洪水就已經有安全去處而不必追蹤。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件入流Vi=10000 m³、出流Vo=7600 m³、儲量增ΔS=2350 m³，殘差R=50 m³，即入流的0.50%。"],"optionsEn":["Top plan area times total depth always equals usable detention storage.","An overflow weir automatically gives excess floodwater a safe destination without route analysis.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event inflow Vi=10000 m³, outflow Vo=7600 m³ and storage increase ΔS=2350 m³."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設事件入流Vi=10000 m³、出流Vo=7600 m³、儲量增ΔS=2350 m³，殘差R=50 m³，即入流的0.50%。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume event inflow Vi=10000 m³, outflow Vo=7600 m³ and storage increase ΔS=2350 m³. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b271-v15-39","title":"數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「數值水量閉合與收斂」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Numerical closure and convergence” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"列出所有水量項與正負號，核對初始儲量、溢流、滲透和反向流是否都有計入。逐次縮小時間步比較最大水位和峰時，再以獨立事件檢查參數，避免只以殘差達標宣告模型有效。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"List all terms with signs, checking initial storage, overflow, infiltration and reversed flow. Progressively reduce time steps to compare maximum stage and peak time, then assess parameters against an independent event rather than declaring validity solely from a small residual. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：製作三種時間步的水量殘差與最大水位比較表，讓其中一種總量相近但漏掉尖峰。說明要保留哪幾項證據，才能同時支持守恆和峰值解析度。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare water residual and maximum stage at three time steps, including one that preserves volume but misses a sharp peak. Identify the evidence needed to support both conservation and adequate resolution of the maximum.","failure":"注意干擾：將未列溢流當數值誤差會掩蓋真實外排，反之把數值殘差當漏水又會誤導維護；只校正總體積而不查水位歷線，可能得到錯誤的池容配置。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Calling omitted overflow numerical error hides actual discharge, while interpreting numerical residual as leakage misdirects maintenance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"列出所有水量項與正負號，核對初始儲量、溢流、滲透和反向流是否都有計入。逐次縮小時間步比較最大水位和峰時，再以獨立事件檢查參數，避免只以殘差達標宣告模型有效。","textEn":"List all terms with signs, checking initial storage, overflow, infiltration and reversed flow. Progressively reduce time steps to compare maximum stage and peak time, then assess parameters against an independent event rather than declaring validity solely from a small residual.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"製作三種時間步的水量殘差與最大水位比較表，讓其中一種總量相近但漏掉尖峰。說明要保留哪幾項證據，才能同時支持守恆和峰值解析度。","textEn":"Compare water residual and maximum stage at three time steps, including one that preserves volume but misses a sharp peak. Identify the evidence needed to support both conservation and adequate resolution of the maximum.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification\"?","options":["列出所有水量項與正負號，核對初始儲量、溢流、滲透和反向流是否都有計入。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","孔口排空時間可永遠用總水量除以一開始的最大出流量。"],"optionsEn":["List all terms with signs, checking initial storage, overflow, infiltration and reversed flow.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Orifice drawdown time always equals total water volume divided by the initial maximum release."],"answer":0,"explanation":"列出所有水量項與正負號，核對初始儲量、溢流、滲透和反向流是否都有計入。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"List all terms with signs, checking initial storage, overflow, infiltration and reversed flow. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b271-v15-40","title":"數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"prerequisiteIds":["b271-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「數值水量閉合與收斂」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Numerical closure and convergence” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將未列溢流當數值誤差會掩蓋真實外排，反之把數值殘差當漏水又會誤導維護；只校正總體積而不查水位歷線，可能得到錯誤的池容配置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Calling omitted overflow numerical error hides actual discharge, while interpreting numerical residual as leakage misdirects maintenance. Calibrating total volume without examining stage trajectories can produce the wrong basin configuration. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例殘差定義為入流減出流再減儲量增加，百分比以總入流作分母；正殘差只表示未解釋水量，並不直接指出物理漏水位置。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A positive residual is unexplained water and does not locate a physical leak.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「模型水量誤差很小，就等於峰值水位和所有設計判斷都正確。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A small model water-balance error proves correct peak stage and every design decision.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b271-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將未列溢流當數值誤差會掩蓋真實外排，反之把數值殘差當漏水又會誤導維護；只校正總體積而不查水位歷線，可能得到錯誤的池容配置。","textEn":"Calling omitted overflow numerical error hides actual discharge, while interpreting numerical residual as leakage misdirects maintenance. Calibrating total volume without examining stage trajectories can produce the wrong basin configuration.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]},{"id":"b271-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「數值水量閉合與收斂機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Numerical closure and convergence mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","將未列溢流當數值誤差會掩蓋真實外排，反之把數值殘差當漏水又會誤導維護；只校正總體積而不查水位歷線，可能得到錯誤的池容配置。","知道總雨量與總面積後，就能唯一決定所需滯洪池容量。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Calling omitted overflow numerical error hides actual discharge, while interpreting numerical residual as leakage misdirects maintenance.","Total rainfall and total area uniquely determine the required detention capacity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將未列溢流當數值誤差會掩蓋真實外排，反之把數值殘差當漏水又會誤導維護；只校正總體積而不查水位歷線，可能得到錯誤的池容配置。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Calling omitted overflow numerical error hides actual discharge, while interpreting numerical residual as leakage misdirects maintenance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-epa-swmmhyd","v15s-dsd-storm","v15s-dsd-taihang","v15s-dsd-happy"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
